Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 23:29:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 034/143] dts: opi4a: translate the DE through the IOMMU
 (mixer0 and display-engine)

The SoC dtsi already gives the mixer iommus = <&iommu 5>. Also attach the
display-engine node (drm->dev) to the same master, so that everything the
DE fetches goes through the IOMMU: the RCQ pool of the mixer and the GEM
scanout buffers alike.

PRIME imports from the GPU (pages that are not physically contiguous) are
then collapsed into one contiguous IOVA by dma_map_sgtable(), which the
compositor swapchain needs: without it gbm_bo_create() failed with
EINVAL.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts    | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
index baf9a9ae8..c458d7c68 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
@@ -632,8 +632,17 @@ &mixer0 {
 	memory-region = <&cma_low>;
 };
 
+/*
+ * DISPLAY BRING-UP: the display-engine (drm->dev) inherits IOMMU master 5
+ * so that scanout GEMs and PRIME imports (kbase, not contiguous)
+ * are allocated/mapped as translated IOVAs. It is the DT equivalent of
+ * the BSP's of_dma_configure(drm->dev, DE_node) (sunxi_de.c:1262): with the
+ * master 5 bypass removed ALL DE traffic is translated, so
+ * an unmapped physical scanout would no longer show.
+ */
 &de {
 	status = "okay";
+	iommus = <&iommu 5>;
 };
 
 &hdmi {
@@ -669,3 +678,10 @@ &display_clocks {
 	assigned-clock-parents = <&ccu CLK_PLL_VIDEO3_4X>;
 	assigned-clock-rates = <600000000>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * DISPLAY BRING-UP: mixer iommus re-enabled (the dtsi already has
+ * iommus = <&iommu 5>). The driver now carries the BSP's v15 recipe
+ * (range invalidation + vendor prefetch) and diagnostic guards
+ * against the corrupt DTE of the boot Oops.
+ */
